al fat areas in the active group decreased significantly compared with those in the control group (Table 2). || Thus, no clinically problematic findings were observed throughout the study in any subject, confirming Table 2 Abdominal fat areas Parameters Values Groups W0 W12 Group-by-time Group Visceral fat (cm 2) Measured Active 127.3 (119.7, 134.9) 121.5 (130.2, 112.8) ** ## Control 119.3 (112.8, 125.8) 120.7 (114.0, 127.4) Change from W0 Active — /C0 5.8 ( /C0 10.0, /C0 1.7) ## Control — 1.4 ( /C0 2.2, 5.1) Subcutaneous fat (cm 2) Measured Active 222.2 (196.9, 247.5) 214.8 (189.4, 240.3) ** # Control 227.8 (204.4, 251.2) 2","Regulation of abdominal adiposity by probiotics Y Kadooka et al 639 European Journal of Clinical Nutrition Table 3 Body weight, BMI, waist and hip circumferences, and waist-to-hip ratio Parameters Values Groups W0 W4 W8 W12 Group-by-time Group Body weight (kg) Measured Active 76.9 (73.8, 79.9) 76.7 (73.7, 79.7) 76.1 (73.1, 79.1) *** 75.8 (72.8, 78.8) *** ### Control 77.1 (73.9, 80.2) 77.0 (73.8, 80.2) 77.3 (74.0, 80.5) 77.4 (74.2, 80.7) Change Active — /C0 0.2 ( /C0 0.4, 0.0) /C0 0.8 ( /C0 1.0, /C0 0.4) *** ### /C0 || Discussion In this study, intake of the probiotic LG2055 showed significant reductions in abdominal visceral and subcuta- neous fat areas, as well as body weight, BMI, waist and hip circumferences, and body fat mass. || Between-group comparisons were performed for the amount Table 1 Baseline characteristics of subjects Parameters Active Control n 43 44 Gender Male 29 30 Female 14 14 Age (year) 48.3 ±9.3 49.2 ±9.1 Height (cm) 166.9 ±9.0 168.0 ±9.1 Body weight (kg) 76.9 ±9.8 77.1 ±10.5 BMI (kg/m 2) 27.5 ±1.7 27.2 ±1.7 Waist circumference (cm) 93.0 ±6.1 93.9 ±5.3 Abdominal visceral fat area (cm 2) 127.3±24.6 119.3 ±21.4 Nutrient intake Energy (kJ/day) 7622.3 ±1139.1 7613.8 ±1489.6 (kcal/day) (1820.9 ±272.1) (1818.9 ±355.9) Protein (g || It is likely that the reductions in waist circumference and body fat mass both reflect a decrease