PMID:41599863,PubMed,41599863,"Efficacy and Safety of CKDB-322, a Combination of",body_fat,"tricornutum daily (n = 50), or a placebo (n = 50).; CKDB-322 supplementation resulted in statistically significant reductions in body fat mass and body fat percentage, as measured by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry (DEXA), compared to the placebo group (p < 0.05).",p < 0.05,,,,,,,n = 50,detail_hint,supplement_queue,pending,,nutrients-18-00250-v2.pdf,1.000,24,Lactiplantibacillus plantarum Q180 and Phaeodactylum tricornutum; Lactiplantibacillus plantarum Q180 and Phaeodacty- lum tricornutum; Lactobacillus; Lactiplantibacillus plantarum; probiotic strains belong to non-pathogenic; probiotic supplementation has emerged as a promising therapeutic approach; probiotic properties,,1.0 × 109 CFU of L. plantarum Q,n = 50; 100 adults,Body Fat; Adiposity; body mass index; BMI; waist circumference; body weight; triglycerides; microbiota; insulin; glucose,"Received: 23 December 2025 Revised: 9 January 2026 Accepted: 11 January 2026 Published: 13 January 2026 Copyright: © 2026 by the authors. Licensee MDPI, Basel, Switzerland. This article is an open access article distributed under the terms and conditions of the Creative Commons Attribution (CC BY) license. Article Efficacy and Safety of CKDB-322, a Combination of Lactiplantibacillus plantarum Q180 and Phaeodactylum tricornutum, for Reducing Body Fat and Abdominal Adiposity in Overweight Adults Hyang-Im Baek 1 , So-Young Kwon 2 , Hye-Ji Noh 2 and Soo Jung Park 3,* 1 Department of Food Science & Nutrition, Woosuk University, Wanju 55338, Republic of Korea; hyangim100@gmail.com 2 Research Institute, Chong Kun Dang Bio (CKD Bio), Seoul 03742, Republic of Korea; ksy2022@ckdbio.com (S.-Y.K.); nhj@ckdbio.com (H.-J.N.) 3 Department of Sasang Constitutional Medicine, College of Korean Medicine, W",Lactiplantibacillus plantarum Q180; Lactiplantibacillus plantarum,CKDB-322; Q180,109 CFU,12 weeks; 12 Week,n = 50; 100 adults; 82 participants; 60 participants; 80 participants; 100 participants; 14 participants; 93 participants; n = 48; n = 45; 91 participants; n = 47,randomized; double-blind; placebo-controlled; clinical trial,diet; powder; capsule,p < 0.05; p > 0.05; p < 0.0001; p = 0.0055; p = 0.0053,"30 kg/m2; 90 cm; 85 cm; decreased significantly in the CKDB-322 group compared to the placebo; increase in the relative abundance of Lactobacillus, suggesting potential modulation of; decreased adipogenesis by downregulating the transcriptional regulators peroxisome proli; reduced body weight gain and adiposity, along with improvements in serum glucose and l; decreased lipogenic markers and enhanced fatty acid oxidation and energy metabolism path; 29.9 kg/m2; 30 kg/m; changes; change of more than 5 percent within one month prior to screening; reduce their daily energy intake by approximately 500 kcal and to follow a carbohydrat; change in body fat mass from baseline to week 12, assessed by dual-energy X-ray absorp; change in body fat mass from baseline; 90%; 20%; changes from baseline were assessed using Pairedt-test when normality assumptions were","Article Efficacy and Safety of CKDB-322, a Combination of Lactiplantibacillus plantarum Q180 and Phaeodactylum tricornutum, for Reducing Body Fat and Abdominal Adiposity in Overweight Adults Hyang-Im Baek 1 , So-Young Kwon 2 , Hye-Ji Noh 2 and Soo Jung Park 3,* 1 Department of Food Science & Nutrition, Woosuk University, Wanju 55338, Republic of Korea; || This randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, 12-week trial evaluated the efficacy and safety of CKDB-322 in overweight adults. || had a body mass index (BMI) of 25–30 kg/m2, and a waist circumference of ≥90 cm for men or ≥85 cm for women. || Results: CKDB-322 supplementation resulted in statistically significant reductions in body fat mass and body fat percentage, as measured by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry (DEXA), compared to the placebo group (p < 0.05). || Computed tomography (CT) analyses also revealed significant reductions in abdominal fat area in the CKDB-322 group ( p < 0.05). || Among metabolic biomark- ers, serum triglycerides and leptin levels decreased significantly in the CKDB-322 group compared to the placebo.","Received: 23 December 2025 Revised: 9 January 2026 Accepted: 11 January 2026 Published: 13 January 2026 Copyright: © 2026 by the authors. Licensee MDPI, Basel, Switzerland. This article is an open access article distributed under the terms and conditions of the Creative Commons Attribution (CC BY) license. Article Efficacy and Safety of CKDB-322, a Combination of Lactiplantibacillus plantarum Q180 and Phaeodactylum tricornutum, for Reducing Body Fat and Abdominal Adiposity in Overweight Adults Hyang-Im Baek 1 , So-Young Kwon 2 , Hye-Ji Noh 2 and Soo Jung Park 3,* 1 Department of Food Science & Nutrition, Woosuk University, Wanju 55338, Republic of Korea; hyangim100@gmail.com 2 Research Insti",ok,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,nutrients-18-00250-v2.pdf,1.000,24,"The primary efficacy endpoint, body fat mass, significantly decreased after 12 weeks of CKDB-322 supplementation compared to baseline (mean change:-1559.19 ± 1500.58 g,p < 0.0001). || The comparison between groups revealed a statistically significant difference (p = 0.0211), indicating that CKDB-322 supplementation helped mitigate the triglyceride increase seen in the placebo group. || Over a 12-week intervention, CKDB-322 supplementation resulted in significant improvements in various adiposity-related outcomes. || plantarum strains have been incorporated into functional foods and dietary supplements because of their strong probiotic properties [27]. || The between-group difference was significant ( p = 0.0086). || However, the difference in change values between the groups did not reach statistical significance (p > 0.05). || placebo: -1.09 ± 1.76%, p = 0.0001), with a significantly larger reduction in the CKDB- 322 group (p = 0.0452). || WHR showed small but statistically significant changes in both groups, with a greater reduction observed in the CKDB-322 group (p = 0.0004).","Hip circumference also decreased significantly in the CKDB-322 group (-1.99 ± 1.20 cm, p < 0.0001), while it increased in the placebo group (0.45 ± 0.86 cm, p = 0.0011), resulting in a significant between-group difference (p < 0.0001). || BMI decreased significantly in the CKDB-322 group ( -0.61 ± 0.66 kg/m2, p < 0.0001), whereas no meaningful change was observed in the placebo group (0.06 ± 0.60 kg/m2, p = 0.5067), resulting in a significant between-group difference (p < 0.0001). || Subcutaneous fat area also decreased significantly in the CKDB-322 group ( -705.06 ± 2932.64 mm 2, p = 0.0028), but did not change signifi- cantly in the placebo group (290.84 ± 2387.70 mm 2, p = 0.2964), resulting in a signif- icant between-group difference ( p = 0.0196). || Waist circum- ference decreased markedly in the CKDB-322 group ( -1.97 ± 1.32 cm, p < 0.0001) but increased significantly in the placebo group (0.55 ± 0.94 cm, p = 0.0003), yielding a strong between-group difference (p < 0.0001). || The CKDB-322 group exhibited substantial decreases in left trunk fat mass (-328.19 ± 493.39 g), while the placebo group showed virtually no change (-9.49 ± 503.04 g), resulting in a significant between- group difference (p = 0.0027). || The primary efficacy endpoint, body fat mass, significantly decreased after 12 weeks of CKDB-322 supplementation compared to baseline (mean change:-1559.19 ± 1500.58 g,p < 0.0001). || The total abdominal fat area significantly decreased in the CKDB- 322 group ( -872.98 ± 3375.92 mm 2, p = 0.0157), while the placebo group showed no significant change (498.16 ± 3047.58 mm2, p = 0.2788). || The between-group difference was significant ( p = 0.0086).","CKDB-322 Group (n = 48) Placebo Group ( n = 45) Group Difference Baseline 12 Week Change Value p-Value (1) Baseline 12 Week Change Value p-Value (1) Mean [95% CI] p-Value (3) DEXA measurement Body fat mass (g) 20,764.52 ± 4429.11 19,205.33 ± 5012.96 -1559.19 ± 1500.58 <0.0001 19,228.18 ± 3824.23 18,564.40 ± 4152.43 -663.78 ± 1523.66 0.0055 -895.4 [-1518.5, -272.3] 0.0053 Body fat percentage (%) 31.17 ± 5.79 29.19 ± 6.29 -1.99 ± 1.68 <0.0001 29.92 ± 5.92 28.83 ± 6.39 -1.09 ± 1.76 0.0001 (2) -0.89 [-1.60, -0.19] 0.04 || (A) Body fat mass, (B) body fat percentage, (C) total abdominal fat area, (D) subcutaneous fat area, (E) BMI, (F) weight, (G) waist circumference, and ( H) hip circumference, ( I) triglycerides, and ( J) leptin in the CKDB-322 and placebo groups at baseline and after 12 weeks of intervention. || Conclusions Twelve weeks of CKDB-322 supplementation resulted in statistically significant reduc- tions in whole-body fat mass, body fat percentage, total abdominal fat area, subcutaneous fat area, and central obesity-related anthropometric indices, including body weight, BMI, waist circumference, hip circumference, and waist-to-hip ratio. || Participants experienced reductions in body fat mass and percentage, as well as decreases in abdominal fat indices (both total and subcutaneous), and key anthropometric measures, including body weight, BMI, waist circumference, hip circumference, and waist-to-hip ratio (WHR). || The primary efficacy endpoint, body fat mass, significantly decreased after 12 weeks of CKDB-322 supplementation compared to baseline (mean change:-1559.19 ± 1500.58 g,p < 0.0001). || CKDB-322 Group (n = 48) Placebo Group ( n = 45) p-Value (1) Sex (M/F) 4/44 6/39 0.5148 (2) Age (years) 36.46 ± 8.32 35.98 ± 9.33 0.8174 Height (cm) 163.41 ± 6.05 161.51 ± 6.73 0.1213 Weight (kg) 72.56 ± 7.20 70.47 ± 6.63 0.1299 BMI (kg/m2) 27.11 ± 1.40 26.98 ± 1.27 0.8175 Waist circumference (cm) 91.08 ± 4.16 90.08 ± 3.81 0.2957 Body fat mass (g) 20,764.52 ± 4429.11 19,228.18 ± 3824.23 0.0776 (3) Values are presented as mean ± SD or number (%). || After 12 weeks, the CKDB-322 group showed significant reductions in body weight (-1.64 ± 1.76 kg, p < 0.0001), while the placebo group showed no significant change (0.14 ± 1.53 kg, p = 0.5426). || The total abdominal fat area significantly decreased in the CKDB- 322 group ( -872.98 ± 3375.92 mm 2, p = 0.0157), while the placebo group showed no significant change (498.16 ± 3047.58 mm2, p = 0.2788).","CKDB-322 Group (n = 48) Placebo Group ( n = 45) p-Value (3) Baseline 12 Week Change Value p-Value (1) Baseline 12 Week Change Value p-Value (1) Lipid profiles Total cholesterol (mg/dL) 195.38 ± 35.00 199.69 ± 32.80 4.31 ± 28.14 0.2937 203.80 ± 35.59 208.91 ± 38.23 5.11 ± 25.16 0.1799 0.8859 Triglyceride (mg/dL) 123.85 ± 73.59 106.38 ± 44.24 -17.48 ± 61.32 0.0884 (2) 122.91 ± 88.12 135.24 ± 102.76 12.33 ± 53.06 0.1858 (2) 0.0211 (4) HDL-C (mg/dL) 53.17 ± 9.28 55.40 ± 9.14 2.23 ± 7.28 0.0063 (2) 56.87 ± 13.85 58.36 ± || In obese mice induced by a high-fat diet, an eight-week administration of CKDB-322 reduced body weight gain, adiposity, and circulating metabolic markers (including glucose, triglycerides, total cholesterol, and leptin) without causing hepatic toxicity. || Serum lipid profiles, including total cholesterol, triglycerides, high-density lipoprotein cholesterol (HDL-C), and low-density lipoprotein cholesterol (LDL-C), were obtained using https://doi.org/10.3390/nu18020250 Nutrients 2026, 18, 250 6 of 24 a standardized automated biochemical analyzer (AU480, Beckman Coulter, Tokyo, Japan). || Additionally, HDL-cholesterol increased significantly in the CKDB-322 group (2.23 ± 7.28 mg/dL, p = 0.0063), although the dif- ference between groups was not statistically significant (p > 0.05). || The comparison between groups revealed a statistically significant difference (p = 0.0211), indicating that CKDB-322 supplementation helped mitigate the triglyceride increase seen in the placebo group. || The between-group difference was significant ( p = 0.0086). || However, the difference in change values between the groups did not reach statistical significance (p > 0.05). || placebo: -1.09 ± 1.76%, p = 0.0001), with a significantly larger reduction in the CKDB- 322 group (p = 0.0452).","However, the increase in Lactobacillus from baseline (∆ value) did not achieve statistical significance between groups (p = 0.0752), despite a similar increasing trend. || In contrast, the relative abundance of Lactobacillus (including Lactiplantibacillus) was significantly higher in the CKDB-322 group compared to the placebo group at week 12 (p = 0.0493). || Results of Microbiome and Short-Chain Fatty Acid Analysis Table 5 and Figure 5 summarize the changes in gut microbiota composition and fecal SCFAs following the 12-week intervention. || These benefits were accompanied by a selective increase inLactobacillusand attenuation of ex- cessive short-chain fatty acid (SCFA) elevations, suggesting that CKDB-322 may influence the gut–adipose metabolic axis. || The between-group difference was significant ( p = 0.0086). || However, the difference in change values between the groups did not reach statistical significance (p > 0.05). || placebo: -1.09 ± 1.76%, p = 0.0001), with a significantly larger reduction in the CKDB- 322 group (p = 0.0452). || WHR showed small but statistically significant changes in both groups, with a greater reduction observed in the CKDB-322 group (p = 0.0004).","This is largely due to safety concerns, adverse effects such as headache, dizziness, and nausea or vomiting, as well as limited long-term tolerability [14–16]. || The between-group difference was significant ( p = 0.0086). || However, the difference in change values between the groups did not reach statistical significance (p > 0.05). || placebo: -1.09 ± 1.76%, p = 0.0001), with a significantly larger reduction in the CKDB- 322 group (p = 0.0452). || WHR showed small but statistically significant changes in both groups, with a greater reduction observed in the CKDB-322 group (p = 0.0004).",week trial evaluated the efficacy and safety of CKDB-322 || reduction [32 || change of more than 5 || week -3 || week 0 || week 6 || wee