PMID:37252684,PubMed,37252684,Effect of green-lipped mussel (,body_fat,"At the baseline, the body fat (BF)% and gynoid fat% were higher in the GSM group compared with the placebo (P < 0⋅05).",,,,,,,,,detail_hint,expansion_queue,pending,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,effect-of-green-lipped-mussel-perna-canaliculus-supplementation-on-faecal-microbiota-body-composition-and-iron-status-markers-in-overweight-and-obese-postmenopausal-women-a-randomised-double-blind-pla.pdf,1.000,12,"Probiotics, prebiotics and nutritional supplements that are used for regulating the microbial communities are proposed as plausible therapeutic options for obesity-related disorders such as metabolic syn- drome and osteoarthritis (OA) (5,6). || 6 journals.cambridge.org/jns https://doi.org/10.1017/jns.2023.41 Published online by Cambridge University Press The baseline levels of some gut microbes including Bacteroides and Clostridium XIVa were different between the GSM and placebo groups which could be due to differences in diet and intake of probiotics or prebiotics as most partici- pants of the study participants reported intake of some type of probiotic products at least once a week in their diet. || However, a previ- ous study reported a notable reduction in Clostridium after GSM supplementation (9). || The dose of 3 g/d was selected as it is achievable through diet (equiva- lent to 1 –2 mussels per day). || (2014) A gut microbiota-targeted diet- ary intervention for amelioration of chronic in ﬂammation under- lying metabolic syndrome. || Restoring the gut microbiota by dietary intervention has been demonstrated to attenuate the chronic in ﬂammation in obese individuals (3). || muciniphila and Biﬁdobacterium, tended to moderately increase after 12 weeks of supplementation with whole GSM powder compared with placebo. || Moreover, the mean dietary iron intake of participants was above the 8 mg/d which is the recommended dietary allow- ance in women over 50 years (50).","The baseline, endp