bnormal or excessive body fat [ 1,2] commonly de ﬁned as a body mass index (BMI) /C21 30 kg/m2, while overweight is de ﬁned as a BMI /C21 25 kg/m2 [3]. || Excessive body adiposity is associated with an increased risk of other diseases such as nonalcoholic fatty liver disease, osteoarthritis, dementia, depression and some types of cancers [ 8e10]. || It has been estimated that above a BMI of 25 kg/ m2, each 5 kg/m 2 increase in BMI is associated on average with an * Corresponding author. || Several interventions can be recommended for the reduction of body adiposity, including dietary modiﬁcations, physical activity, behavioral changes, pharmacological treatment, and bariatric surgery [ 14].","Narrative Review Randomized controlled trials reporting the effects of probiotics in individuals with overweight and obesity: A critical review of the interventions and body adiposity parameters Marcella Rodrigues Guedes a, Karine Scanci da Silva Pontes a, Maria In ^es Barreto Silva b, c, Mario Fritsch Neves d,M /C19arcia Regina Simas Torres Klein b, * a Post-Graduation Program in Clinical and Experimental Pathophysiology, State University of Rio de Janeiro (UERJ), Rio de Janeiro, Brazil b Department of Applied Nutrition, Nutrition Institute, State University of Rio de Janeiro (UERJ), Rio de Janeiro, Brazil c Human Nutrition Research Unit, Department of Agricultural, Food and Nutritional Sci",ok,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Randomized controlled trials reporting the effects of probiotics in individuals with overweight and obesity_ A critical review o(科研通-ablesci.com) (1).pdf,1.000,13,"The three RCTs that evaluated the effects of probiotics supple- mentation with a longer duration (24 weeks), with a probiotics dose of at least 10 10, using probiotics in capsules/sachet/powder and without dietary intervention, observed a signiﬁcant decrease in body weight and all other outcomes of body adiposity [ 18,75,76]. || Additionally, the bene ﬁcial effects of probiotics were more consistent in trials with /C21 12 weeks, dose of probiotics /C21 1010 CFU/day, probiotics in capsules, sachets or powder and pro- biotics supplementation without concomitant energy restriction. || The four most prominent features of the studies associated with bene ﬁ cial effects of probiotics were duration of at least 12 weeks, a dose of probiotics /C21 1010 CFU/day, supplementation of probiotics in capsules, sachets or powder and supplementation without the association with energy restriction. || Clinical Nutrition 42 (2023) 835 e847 842 beneﬁcial results of probiotics when the interventions were char- acterized by /C21 12 weeks duration, probiotics dose /C21 1010 CFU/day, in capsules, sachets or powder, and without concomitant energy restriction, and the outcome measures included assessment of body adiposity deposits by evaluating body fat mass and waist circumference, instead of body weight and BMI. || Characteristics of the studies Reduction P a Signiﬁcant Non signi ﬁcant Body Weight (kg) Duration of the study (weeks) /C21 12 (n ¼ 18) 9 (50%) 9 (50%) 0.007 <12 (n ¼ 10) 0 (0%) 10 (100%) Dose of probiotics (CFU/day) /C21 1010 (n ¼ 19) 7 (37%) 12 (63%) 0.477 < 1010 (n ¼ 5) 1 (20%) 4 (80%) Vehicle of probiotic Capsule/Powder (n ¼ 15) 7 (47%) 8 (53%) 0.030 Dairy (n ¼ 12) 1 (8%) 11 (92%) Energy restriction Yes (n ¼ 9) 1 (11%) 8 (89%) 0.136 No (n ¼ 18) 7 (39%) 11 (61%) Number of species /C21 2( n ¼ 15) 4 (27%) 11 (73%) || The bene ﬁcial effects of probiotics were more consistent in trials with /C21 12 weeks, probiotics dose /C21 10 10 CFU/day, in capsules, sachets or powder, and without concomitant energy restriction. || Clinical Nutrition 42 (2023) 835 e847 839 Table 1 (continued ) Author Year, Location Population (Design) Baseline characteristics (Probiotic/control) Sample size (PB/C) Duration (weeks:w or days:d) Probiotics Control group Dietary intervention Methods for assessment of body adiposity Main outcomes BMI (Kg/ m 2) Age (years) Sex %F Strains Dose (CFU/ day) Vehicle L. || Author