EUROPEPMC:40218949,PubMed,40218949,"A 12-Week, Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of",body_fat,"A 12-Week, Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of This study aims to evaluate the efficacy and safety of probiotics for body fat reduction in obese individuals.; A total of 106 participants with a body mass index between 25 and 30 kg/m2 were randomly assigned to either the experimental group treating with Lactobacillus plantarum LMT1-48 or the placebo group in the placebo-controlled clinical trial.",p = 0.009; p = 0.004,,,,,,,106 participants,detail_hint,expansion_queue,pending,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,nutrients-17-01191.pdf,1.000,15,"(5) Administered probiotics, prebiotics, or a probiotic product on a continuous basis (4 or more times per week) within 2 weeks of Visit 1. || Data shown and error bars are mean ± SD (non-parametric t-test, *** p < 0.001). || Data shown and erro r bars are mean ± SD (non-parametric t-test, *** p < 0.001). || Moreover, there was no statistically significant difference in the intake of IP between the case and control groups (p = 0.590), with the case group’s mean compliance being 96.18± 7.47% and the con- trol group’s being 95.36± 8.04%. || reuteri NCIMB 30242 (5 × 1010 CFU) in a yogurt formulation by healthy individuals [ 37] and L. || plantarum LMT1-48 holds potential as a novel probiotic to mitigate body weight gain and/or diet-induced obesity. || If conservative treatments such as diet and exercise do not result in a loss of 10% of the existing body weight after 3–6 months, medication may be considered [10]. || Participants in the experimental group were instructed to take two capsules of 500 mg (total amount of LMT1-48 is 5 × 109 CFU) once a day for 12 weeks while drinking water [15,16].","Results: After 12 weeks of follow-up period, the body fat mass decreased significantly, from 30.0 ± 4.4 to 28.3 ± 4.1 kg in the experimental group (p = 0.009). || Moreover, there was no statistically significant difference in the intake of IP between the case and control groups (p = 0.590), with the case group’s mean compliance being 96.18± 7.47% and the con- trol group’s being 95.36± 8.04%. || Comparing the results from baseline to 12 weeks, the experimental group was significantly reduced in body fat mass of the trunk, android, gynoid, and both legs. || Body fat mass decreased significantly in the experimental group by 1.6 ± 1.9 kg compared with the placebo group, where it decreased by 0.7 ± 2.2 kg (p = 0.009). || Moreover, body fat percentage decreased significantly in the case group by 1.5 ± 2.0% compared with the placebo group, where it decreased by 0.4 ± 2.1% (p = 0.004). || Data shown and error bars are mean ± SD (non-parametric t-test, *** p < 0.001). || Data shown and erro r bars are mean ± SD (non-parametric t-test, *** p < 0.001). || For weighted UniFrac distances, post-treatment intra-group distances significantly increased in the experimental group but decreased in the placebo group.","LMT1-48 (n = 53) Placebo (n = 53) p-Value Gender (Male) 21 (39.6) 18 (34.0) 0.546 Age 44.6 ± 12.9 40.7 ± 10.2 0.084 Height (cm) 166.3 ± 8.3 166.7 ± 9.3 0.780 Weight (kg) 75.5 ± 8.2 75.3 ± 9.6 0.762 BMI (kg/m2) 27.3 ± 1.3 27.0 ± 1.3 0.303 SBP (mmHg) 126.0 ± 13.4 117.9 ± 12.2 0.002 DBP (mmHg) 75.3 ± 9.9 71.8 ± 11.6 0.043 Glucose (mg/dL) 86.7 ± 8.3 85.8 ± 9.2 0.205 Total cholesterol (mg/dL) 208.8 ± 34.6 198.4 ± 30.5 0.104 Triglyceride (mg/dL) 136.9 ± 136.8 111.1 ± 57.4 0.825 HDL cholesterol (mg/dL) 55.6 ± 15.0 52.1 ± || Changes in body weight, thigh circumference, arm circumference, hip circumference, waist circumference, waist/hip ratio, BMI, lean body mass and body fat percentage by DEXA, visceral fat, subcutaneous fat, total abdominal fat area, and visceral/subcutaneous fat area ratio, measured by computed tomography (TOSHIBA SCANNER Activation 1, TOSHIBA, Tokyo, Japan), were among the secondary efficacy evaluations. || Group Baseline Week 12 p-Value † p-Value ‡ Body fat mass (kg) LMT1-48 30.0 ± 4.4 28.3 ± 4.1 <0.001 0.009 Placebo 29.0 ± 4.4 28.3 ± 4.3 0.020 Body fat percentage (%) LMT1-48 40.9 ± 6.8 39.4 ± 6.3 <0.001 0.004 Placebo 39.7 ± 5.8 39.3 ± 5.8 0.229 Lean mass (kg) LMT1-48 41.9 ± 8.5 42.1 ± 8.1 0.388 0.026 Placebo 42.5 ± 8.2 42.2 ± 8.4 0.061 Visceral fat area (cm2) LMT1-48 129.7 ± 43.8 120.9 ± 43.7 <0.001 0.368 Placebo 112.2 ± 34.5 107.0 ± 33.4 0.017 Subcutaneous fat area (cm2) LMT1-48 236.8 ± 57.0 222.2 ± 61.8 <0.001 0.1 || Results: After 12 weeks of follow-up period, the body fat mass decreased significantly, from 30.0 ± 4.4 to 28.3 ± 4.1 kg in the experimental group (p = 0.009). || Body fat mass decreased significantly in the experimental group by 1.6 ± 1.9 kg compared with the placebo group, where it decreased by 0.7 ± 2.2 kg (p = 0.009). || Comparing the results from baseline to 12 weeks, the experimental group was significantly reduced in body fat mass of the trunk, android, gynoid, and both legs. || Compared with the placebo group, the experimental group suggested a decrease in body fat mass and body fat percentage from baseline to after 12 weeks, which is statistically significant. || Discussion When compared with the placebo group, 12-week consumption with LMT1-48 signifi- cantly decreased body fat mass and body fat percentage and enhanced lean mass through our trial.","LMT1-48 (n = 53) Placebo (n = 53) p-Value Gender (Male) 21 (39.6) 18 (34.0) 0.546 Age 44.6 ± 12.9 40.7 ± 10.2 0.084 Height (cm) 166.3 ± 8.3 166.7 ± 9.3 0.780 Weight (kg) 75.5 ± 8.2 75.3 ± 9.6 0.762 BMI (kg/m2) 27.3 ± 1.3 27.0 ± 1.3 0.303 SBP (mmHg) 126.0 ± 13.4 117.9 ± 12.2 0.002 DBP (mmHg) 75.3 ± 9.9 71.8 ± 11.6 0.043 Glucose (mg/dL) 86.7 ± 8.3 85.8 ± 9.2 0.205 Total cholesterol (mg/dL) 208.8 ± 34.6 198.4 ± 30.5 0.104 Triglyceride (mg/dL) 136.9 ± 136.8 111.1 ± 57.4 0.825 HDL cholesterol (mg/dL) 55.6 ± 15.0 52.1 ± || Group Baseline Week 12 p-Value † p-Value ‡ Total cholesterol (mg/dL) 