bese women with food addiction: a randomized clinical trial Elham Narmaki , Mohaddeseh Borazjani , Asal Ataie-Jafari , Nastaran Hariri , Azita Hekmat Doost , Mostafa Qorbani & Atoosa Saidpour To cite this article: Elham Narmaki , Mohaddeseh Borazjani , Asal Ataie-Jaf",ok,,"The combined effects of probiotics and restricted calorie diet on the anthropometric indices, eating behavior, and hormone level(科研通-ablesci.com).pdf",0.873,14,"Each probiotic supplement contained six species of probiotic bacteria [Lactobacillus acidophi- lus (1.8 × 10 9 CFU/capsule), Biﬁdobacterium bi ﬁdum (1.8 × 109 CFU/capsule), Biﬁdobacterium lactis (1.8 × 109 CFU/capsule), Biﬁdobacterium longum (1.8 × 109 CFU/capsule), Lactobacillus rhamnosus (1 × 109 CFU/ capsule), Lactobacillus reuteri (1 × 109 CFU/capsule), magnesium stearate, and maltodextrin], and the placebo supplement contained starch. || Nevertheless, the reduction of the appetite score was sig- niﬁcantly higher in the probiotic group than in the pla- cebo group ( p < 0.001). || In addition, serum oxytocin levels increased signiﬁ- cantly only in the probiotic group as compared to the baseline ( p < 0.001), and this increment was signi ﬁcant in comparison with the placebo group ( p = 0.02). || Also, the cognitive restriction score signiﬁcantly increased in the probiotic group at the end of the study compared to the baseline ( p < 0.001), whereas no signi ﬁcant change was observed in the pla- cebo group ( p = 0.7). || Moreover, leptin level signi ﬁcantly decreased in the probiotic group compared to the baseline values ( p < 0.001), while probiotics did not cause a greater signiﬁcant reduction in leptin level, compared to the placebo group. || Consistent with our results, some recent meta-analyses conducted on var- ious populations including individuals with obesity, dia- betes mellitus, metabolic syndrome, and non-alcoholic fatty liver disease reported that supplementation with probiotics might have a minor, but signi ﬁcant favorable eﬀect on fat mass and body weight reduction [ 28– 31,51,52]. || Do probiotics, prebiotics and synbiotics aﬀect adiponectin and leptin in adults? || However, the reductions of these scores were signi ﬁ- cantly higher in the probiotic group than in the placebo group ( p < 0.001).","Also, the cognitive restriction score signiﬁcantly increased in the probiotic group at the end of the study compared to the baseline ( p < 0.001), whereas no signi ﬁcant change was observed in the pla- cebo group ( p = 0.7). || In addition, serum oxytocin levels increased signiﬁ- cantly only in the probiotic group as compared to the baseline ( p < 0.001), and this increment was signi ﬁcant in comparison with the placebo group ( p = 0.02). || Moreover, leptin level signi ﬁcantly decreased in the probiotic group compared to the baseline values ( p < 0.001), while probiotics did not cause a greater signiﬁcant reduction in leptin level, compared to the placebo group. || Results: Probiotics administration signi ﬁcantly reduced weight, body mass index (BMI), waist circumference (WC), waist to hip ratio (WHR), bod y fat percentage (BFP), and trunk fat percentage (TFP) compared to the placebo group ( p < 0.001). || Also, no signi ﬁcant within or between-group diﬀerences were seen in terms ofﬁber and protein intake, and no signi ﬁcant changes were observed in physical activity levels between the two groups at the baseline (p = 0.4) and during the study ( p =0 . || Also, a signiﬁ cant improvement was observed in eating behavior in the probiotic group compared to the placebo group ( p < 0.001).Serum levels of oxytocin increased and NPY decreased signiﬁcantly in the probiotic group compared to the placebo group ( p =0 . || Results with P < 0.05 were considered as statisti- cally signi ﬁcant. || There was no signi ﬁcant diﬀerence in leptin changes between the two groups ( p = 0.1).","Results: Probiotics administration signi ﬁcantly reduced weight, body mass index (BMI), waist circumference (WC), waist to 