ained a challenge [2]. || Meta- bolic hormones such as leptin, oxytocin, and neuropeptide Y (NPY) can not only regulate mechan- isms involved in the homeostatic food consumption such as appetite, food intake, and energy expenditure, but can also a ﬀect the hedonic drive for food [16 – 18]. || GM may also inﬂ uence the host eat- ing behavior by a ﬀecting appetite and hormone levels [23]. || So far, few studies have investigated the e ﬀects of probiotics on appetite-regulating hormones [ 32–34] and eating behaviors [35 –37].","Full Terms & Conditions of access and use can be found at https://www.tandfonline.com/action/journalInformation-journalCode=ynns20 Nutritional Neuroscience An International Journal on Nutrition, Diet and Nervous System ISSN: (Print) (Online) Journal homepage: https://www.tandfonline.com/loi/ynns20 The combined effects of probiotics and restricted calorie diet on the anthropometric indices, eating behavior, and hormone levels of obese women with food addiction: a randomized clinical trial Elham Narmaki , Mohaddeseh Borazjani , Asal Ataie-Jafari , Nastaran Hariri , Azita Hekmat Doost , Mostafa Qorbani & Atoosa Saidpour To cite this article: Elham Narmaki , Mohaddeseh Borazjani , Asal Ataie-Jaf",ok,,Lactobacillus acidophi-; Lactobacillus rhamnosus; Lactobacillus reuteri,,10 9 CFU; 109 CFU,12 weeks; 1 month; 2 months; 6 Week; 8 weeks,n = 62; 62 women; n = 31; 62 participants,randomized; clinical trial; double-blind; placebo-controlled,Diet; capsules; supplement; capsule,p < 0.001; p = 0.002; P < 0.05; p = 0.7; p = 0.1; p = 0.03; p = 0.02; p = 0.04; p = 0.005; p = 0.05; p = 0.4,"reduced weight, body mass index (BMI), waist circumference (WC), waist to hip ratio (WHR), bod y; improvement was observed in eating behavior in the probiotic group compared to the placebo group; increased and NPY decreased signiﬁcantly in the probiotic group compared to the placebo group ( p; decreased in the probiotic group compared to the baseline values ( p < 0; 19%; 71%; 12.2%; 6.4%; reduced diversity and increased capacity in energy absorption [24 ]; improve eating behavior and obesity management in people with FA; 2.4 Kg; 80%; 20%; 39.99 kg/m; 30 kg/m; 35 kg/; 39.9 kg/m2; reduced by ∼300–500Kcal to reach weight loss","Submit your article to this journal Article views: 15 View related articles View Crossmark data The combined e ﬀects of probiotics and restricted calorie diet on the anthropometric indices, eating behavior, and hormone levels of obese women with food addiction: a randomized clinical trial Elham Narmaki a, Mohaddeseh Borazjani b, Asal Ataie-Jafari c, Nastaran Hariri a, Azita Hek || Results: Probiotics administration signi ﬁcantly reduced weight, body mass index (BMI), waist circumference (WC), waist to hip ratio (WHR), bod y fat percentage (BFP), and trunk fat percentage (TFP) compared to the placebo group ( p < 0.001). || Widespread e ﬀorts for obesity pre- vention and treatment have had partial achievements over a long time, and sustainable weight loss has remained a challenge [2]. || The sample size was determined based on the detection of a di ﬀerence of 2.4 Kg in body weight with a power of 80% and α = 0.05 [35 ]. || Women aged 20 –50 years old, with a body mass index (BMI) of 30 –39.99 kg/m 2, and a diagnosis of FA by the Yale Food Addiction Scale (YFAS) questionnaire [38] were included. || (c) adherence to the weight loss plan over the previous 2 months; || Strati ﬁcation was performed based on BMI distri- bution (two levels: 30 kg/m 2 ≤ BMI < 35, and 35 kg/ m2 ≤ BMI ≤ 39.9 kg/m2).","Full Terms & Conditions of access and use can be found at https://www.tandfonline.com/action/journalInformation-journalCode=ynns20 Nutritional Neuroscience An International Journal on Nutrition, Diet and Nervous System ISSN: (Print) (Online) Journal homepage: https://www.tandfonline.com/loi/ynns20 The combined effects of probiotics and restricted calorie diet on the anthropometric indices, eating behavior, and hormone levels of obese women with food addiction: a randomized clinical trial Elham Narmaki , Mohaddeseh Borazjani , Asal Ataie-Jafari , Nastaran Hariri , Azita Hekmat Doost , Mostafa Qorbani & Atoosa Saidpour To cite this article: Elham Narmaki , Mohaddeseh Borazjani , Asal Ataie-Jaf",ok,,"The combined effects of probiotics and restricted calorie diet on the anthropometric indices, eating behavior, and hormone level(科研通-ablesci.com).pdf",0.873,14,"Each probiotic supplement contained six species of probiotic bacteria [Lactobacillus acidophi- lus (1.8 × 10 9 CFU/capsule), Biﬁdobacterium bi ﬁdum (1.8 × 109 CFU/capsule), Biﬁdobacterium lactis (1.8 × 109 CFU/capsule), Biﬁdobacterium longum (1.8 × 109 CFU/capsule), Lactobacillus rhamnosus (1 × 109 CFU/ capsule), Lactobacillus reuteri (1 × 109 CFU/capsule), magnesium stearate, and maltodextrin], and the placebo supplement contained starch. || Nevertheless, the reduction of the appetite score was sig- niﬁcantly higher in the probiotic group than in the pla- cebo group ( p < 0.001). || In addition, serum oxytocin levels increased signiﬁ- cantly only in the probiotic group as compared to the baseline ( p < 0.001), and this increment was signi ﬁcant in comparison with the placebo group ( p = 0.02). || Also, the cognitive restriction score signiﬁcantly increased in the probiotic group at the end of the study compared to the baseline ( p < 0.001), whereas no signi ﬁcant change was observed in the pla- cebo group ( p = 0.7). || Moreover, leptin level signi ﬁcantly decreased in the probiotic group compared to the baseline values ( p < 0.001), while probiotics did not cause a greater signiﬁcant reduction in leptin level, compared to the placebo group. || Consistent with our results, some recent meta-analyses conducted on var- ious populations including individuals with obesity, dia- betes mellitus, metabolic syndrome, and non-alcoholic fatty liver disease reported that supplementation with probiotics might have a minor, but signi ﬁcant favorable eﬀect on fat mass and body weight reduction [ 28– 31,51,52]. || Do probiotics, prebiotics and synbiotics aﬀect adiponectin and leptin in adults? || However, the reductions of these scores were signi ﬁ- cantly higher in the probiotic group than in the placebo group ( p < 0.001).","Also, the cognitive restriction score signiﬁcantly increased in the probiotic group at the end of the study compared to the baseline ( p < 0.001), whereas no signi ﬁcant change was observed in the pla- cebo group ( p = 0.7). || In addition, serum oxytocin levels increased signiﬁ- cantly only in the probiotic group as compared to the baseline ( p < 0.001), and this increment was signi ﬁcant in comparison with the placebo group ( p = 0.02). || Moreover, leptin level signi ﬁcantly decreased in the probiotic group compared to the baseline values ( p < 0.001), while probiotics did not cause a greater signiﬁcant reduction in leptin level, compared to the placebo group. || Results: Probiotics administration signi ﬁcantly reduced weight, body mass index (BMI), waist circumference (WC), waist to hip ratio (WHR), bod y fat percentage (BFP), and trunk fat percentage (TFP) compared to the placebo group ( p < 0.001). || Also, no signi ﬁcant within or between-group diﬀerences were seen in terms ofﬁber and protein intake, and no signi ﬁcant changes were observed in physical activity levels between the two groups at the baseline (p = 0.4) and during the study ( p =0 . || Also, a signiﬁ cant improvement was observed in eating behavior in the probiotic group compared to the placebo group ( p < 0.001).Serum levels of oxytocin increased and NPY decreased signiﬁcantly in the probiotic group compared to the placebo group ( p =0 . || Results with P < 0.05 were considered as statisti- cally signi ﬁcant. || There was no signi ﬁcant diﬀerence in leptin changes between the two groups ( p = 0.1).","Results: Probiotics administration signi ﬁcantly reduced weight, body mass index (BMI), waist circumference (WC), waist to h